From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:20:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: ath12k: open one WMI endpoint for the single-MAC
 QCN9274 firmware

On a QCN9274 hw2.0 whose MHI firmware image is the single-MAC one (an
unset OTP board ID without qcom,split-phy, as on the Arista C-460's three
single-band QCN9224 radios), ath12k still opened two WMI endpoints, so
start-up stopped at "HTC Service WMI MAC1 connect request failed: 0x1",
then "failed to start core: -110". Open one in that case.

The same was reported for the Wallys DR9574 (ath12k list, May 2026,
kernel bugzilla 221550); no fix had been posted.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile              |  2 +-
 ...-for-the-single-MAC-QCN9274-firmware.patch | 69 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath12k/980-wifi-ath12k-open-one-WMI-endpoint-for-the-single-MAC-QCN9274-firmware.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
index 4902e2e7969..dc7d96a1e27 100644
--- a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ PKG_NAME:=mac80211
 
 PKG_SOURCE_VERSION:=7.2
 PKG_VERSION:=$(subst -,_,$(PKG_SOURCE_VERSION))
-PKG_RELEASE:=40
+PKG_RELEASE:=41
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0-only
 PKG_LICENSE_FILES:=COPYING
 
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath12k/980-wifi-ath12k-open-one-WMI-endpoint-for-the-single-MAC-QCN9274-firmware.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath12k/980-wifi-ath12k-open-one-WMI-endpoint-for-the-single-MAC-QCN9274-firmware.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..3b114d58728
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath12k/980-wifi-ath12k-open-one-WMI-endpoint-for-the-single-MAC-QCN9274-firmware.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:15:00 -0600
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: open one WMI endpoint for the single-MAC
+ QCN9274 firmware
+
+ath12k_htc_init() sizes the WMI endpoints from the preferred hardware
+mode, which is not known yet when it runs, so QCN9274 hw2.0 falls back to
+hw_params->max_radios, two. When ath12k_mhi_register() has picked the
+single-MAC firmware image (an unset or erased OTP board ID without
+qcom,split-phy, or a valid one without the dual-MAC bit), that firmware
+offers no WMI MAC1 service and start-up stops:
+
+  HTC Service WMI MAC1 connect request failed: 0x1)
+  failed to connect to WMI CONTROL service status: -71
+  failed to receive wmi unified ready event: -110
+  failed to start core: -110
+
+Seen on the three single-band QCN9224 (17cb:1109, qcn9274 hw2.0) radios
+of the Arista C-460, whose OTP board ID is unset. The same was reported
+for the Wallys DR9574's single-band QCN9274 hw2.0 cards (ath12k list,
+May 2026, kernel bugzilla 221550).
+
+Remember which image was chosen and open a single WMI endpoint when it is
+the single-MAC one.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
+@@ -1146,6 +1146,8 @@ struct ath12k_base {
+ 	struct ath12k_hw_group *ag;
+ 	struct ath12k_wsi_info wsi_info;
+ 	enum ath12k_firmware_mode fw_mode;
++	/* the MHI firmware image chosen is the dual-MAC one */
++	bool dualmac;
+ 	struct ath12k_ftm_event_obj ftm_event_obj;
+ 	bool hw_group_ref;
+ 
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+@@ -222,6 +222,8 @@ int ath12k_mhi_register(struct ath12k_pc
+ 		}
+ 	}
+ 
++	ab->dualmac = dualmac;
++
+ 	if (dualmac) {
+ 		if (ab->fw.amss_dualmac_data && ab->fw.amss_dualmac_len > 0) {
+ 			/* use MHI firmware file from firmware-N.bin */
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/htc.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/htc.c
+@@ -773,7 +773,14 @@ int ath12k_htc_init(struct ath12k_base *
+ 		htc->wmi_ep_count = 3;
+ 		break;
+ 	default:
+-		htc->wmi_ep_count = ab->hw_params->max_radios;
++		/* The hardware mode is not known yet. A QCN9274 hw2.0 running
++		 * the single-MAC firmware image offers no WMI MAC1 service, so
++		 * asking for max_radios endpoints fails the whole start-up.
++		 */
++		if (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_QCN9274_HW20 && !ab->dualmac)
++			htc->wmi_ep_count = 1;
++		else
++			htc->wmi_ep_count = ab->hw_params->max_radios;
+ 		break;
+ 	}
+ 
-- 
